{
  "reasoning_summary": "Most teen girls use social media but post publicly infrequently; lurking/consuming is more common than sharing, so the modal posting categories are 'less than once a week' and 'a few times a week', with a substantial share posting almost never and a smaller daily-posting group. For negative comparison, teen girls skew toward 'sometimes' with a meaningful 'often' tail and relatively few saying 'never'. The two items are modestly positively associated: more frequent posters/heavier engagers report somewhat more upward comparison, though many low-posting 'lurkers' also report it, so the association is weak rather than strong.",
  "joint_probabilities": [
    [0.067, 0.087, 0.092, 0.034],
